xsf: special function kernels from SciPy
========================================

Upstream:   https://github.com/scipy/xsf
Commit:     f7b85f505a94fd398024478d2e747b01dd2d7a6d
Pinned by:  SciPy v1.18.1 (e4e854eaa8f18d807cd3496028e257e36caa93cc),
            through its subprojects/xsf gitlink
Licence:    BSD-3-Clause (xsf/LICENSE), with bundled code under the
            licences listed in xsf/LICENSES_bundled.txt and inst/COPYRIGHTS

Vendored:   include/xsf/** as xsf/include/xsf/, plus LICENSE and
            LICENSES_bundled.txt
Excluded:   include/xsf/numpy.h (includes Python.h and NumPy headers)
            include/xsf/third_party/ (mdspan, reached only from numpy.h)

Patches:    tools/patches/*.patch, applied in order by tools/vendor/vendor-xsf.
            Every other file is byte-identical to upstream. The checksums of
            the patched tree are in tools/vendor/checksums.sha256, and
            tools/vendor/verify checks them.

  0001-float-to-int-conversion.patch (2026-10-24)
            cephes/beta.h, faddeeva.h: guard float-to-int conversions of
            NaN and out-of-range doubles, undefined behaviour that clang's
            UBSan (and CRAN's UBSan check) reports; behaviour is otherwise
            unchanged. Reported upstream as scipy/xsf#338
            (https://github.com/scipy/xsf/issues/338). Drop it when a SciPy
            release's xsf includes a fix.

  0002-bessel-float-to-int-conversion.patch (2026-10-24)
            bessel.h, cephes/yv.h, amos/amos.h: three more conversions of
            out-of-range doubles to int that the Bessel xsref inputs reach;
            behaviour unchanged below 2^31, SciPy's values kept above it.
            Added to scipy/xsf#338.

  0003-amos-order-to-int.patch (2026-10-27)
            amos/amos.h: the eleven other conversions of the order to int.
            Outside int range or for NaN they now give INT_MIN, what x86-64
            gives, so arm64 matches SciPy on x86-64 for orders of 2^31 or
            more, and UBSan has nothing to report. Added to scipy/xsf#338.

Update procedure
----------------
1. tools/vendor/vendor-xsf <scipy-tag>   (a SciPy release tag, e.g. v1.19.0);
   if a patch no longer applies, check whether upstream fixed it and drop it
2. tools/vendor/verify
3. Update this file's commit lines, then run the full test suite, including
   the xsref and SciPy-value tables, before merging.

The pin follows SciPy releases rather than xsf tags, so that zuspecial's
values match a SciPy users can install (design.md section 8 and 16).
